WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
All right, everyone calm down. "YouTube Heroes" isn't the worst idea ever.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.540
It's just a middle-of-the-road idea with good intentions that fails to read the optics of the situation and

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.260
inadvertently insults most of the content creators on YouTube.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:17.820
[Intro music plays]

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:23.700
Before we can start, let's make sure that everyone is up to speed on what exactly 'YouTube Heroes' is.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.740
Late in the evening on September 20th,

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.760
YouTube unveiled a new program that would be starting up in the vague near future called 'YouTube Heroes'.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:38.780
The program would reward participants with points for activities such as correctly reporting community standards violating content, adding subtitles,

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:44.840
captions, and descriptions to videos and participating in the "YouTube Heroes" section of the YouTube Creators Community.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:49.640
Which I think I need to explain because I'm pretty sure you've never heard of it before.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:55.660
So, YouTube has its own forum called "YouTube creators community" found at the horrifying URL

00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:00.400
[www.youtube-creatorcommunity.com]

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:07.020
It is so poorly faced that it doesn't even show up in the first page of Google searches for "YouTube Creator Community",

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:13.380
and Google owns it! In fact, to get there organically you have to go to [youtube.com/yt/creators],

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:18.180
and then it's not at the top navigation bar, nor is it in the footer. You need to follow a link in the body

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.540
of the page to the 'Creator Community',

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:27.840
where you are immediately served with an error message saying "Node not found". I am not joking. This is not a joke!

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.480
Well, it is a joke, but not "that" kind of joke.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.120
Whatever. Okay.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:41.040
So, YouTube heroes community is intended to be a subsection of the impossible to reach YouTube Creators Community site...

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.826
and it's just a forum. That's literally all it is.

00:01:43.826 --> 00:01:49.000
It functions almost exactly like 'Discourse' or a text only 'subReddit' or 'Yahoo! answers'

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.380
People post stuff, and there's upvotes.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.340
So by participating in these three key areas,

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.046
flagging content like pornography or animal abuse,

00:01:57.046 --> 00:02:00.780
submitting subtitles and captions, and posting on the heroes forum,

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.799
you will earn points, and earning points in turn confers privileges.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.780
It's an RPG leveling system.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.769
Transparently, the whole thing is an attempt at gamifying the more monotonous aspects of YouTube,

00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:13.540
so we're just going to describe it like a video game.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.220
I mean they called it "Youtube Heroes", for God's sake!

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.880
At the lowest level Heroes have scrub class features like access to the dashboard and forums.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.940
At level 2, which only requires

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:29.240
10 Xp heroes unlock workshops and live hangouts so basically a knowledge base like whatever

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:34.040
This is barely a reward. At level 3 is when things catch people's attention

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:41.320
Access to so called super tools like the ability to mass flag content for standard violations and the ability to Moderate community content

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:47.130
That right there is what's got a lot of people up in arms, but it's not site-wide comment moderation power.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:53.820
It's only moderation power on the YouTube heroes community; that bad, hard-to-find, forgotten forum that I mentioned earlier.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:03:00.600
Also the Mass Flagging tool still requires that a human at YouTube confirms the content for Community violations,

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.440
just the same as if you reported them one by one right now.

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.259
We'll discuss the implications of all of these in a bit.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:13.679
So moving on. Level 4 at 400 XP unlocks sneak previews of upcoming YouTube features and the

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:20.819
contentious vague promise of a direct line to actual flesh-and-blood humans working at YouTube. Put a pin in that one too.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:26.670
Level 5 at a whopping thousand XP gives. You access to product beta tests, essentially allowing you to do even more

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:31.530
unpaid work for YouTube, and the ability to apply for the hero summit which is a

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.369
party, probably in Anaheim almost certainly in California.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:40.920
And you're likely responsible for getting yourself there and back again and probably finding a place to stay too.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:47.130
So, onto the contentious parts. First the super tools. These are the kind of things that sound good

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.130
But don't really do anything meaningful.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.999
It's a tiny amount of sequestered power - the mod powers on the forums could be abused,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.279
but it's a forum no one really cares about anyway.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:02.729
So the worst case scenario is some weird niche internet drama where a power-hungry mod goes on a deleting spree before being stripped and banned

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.660
an hour later. I mean, it's still a bad idea

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.380
but it's not a monumentally awful idea.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:13.859
The mass flagging tool is ripe for abuse but it's not an abuse that creators are likely to see in ways that they don't already.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:17.669
Obsessive stalkers will already chain report all of your videos.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.560
This is technically making harassment slightly easier,

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:28.280
but it's already so easy to harass people on YouTube that it's not worth the effort to get to level 3 just to save yourself the clicks.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:31.580
You could spend time submitting subtitles just to level up

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.920
or you could spend that time filing false reports and making burner accounts to file more false reports

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.830
Still though this one does give me the biggest pause because even disregarding the mass flagging tool

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:44.740
it is actively incentivizing flagging videos for content violations.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:49.740
And the higher the volume of videos reported the more false positives.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.360
By incentivizing the system

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.199
there's a good chance that they're going to draw the attention of bad actors in greater numbers

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.500
So while it doesn't make it any easier to be awful on YouTube

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:03.620
(because it's already super easy to be awful on YouTube)

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:07.100
there is a chance that it will make awfulness a bit more common.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:10.340
And finally the direct line to human beings at YouTube.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.040
The simple reality is that this is going to be a dead end.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:17.280
I fully expect that anyone who manages to reach this level is going to find that line

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:20.920
woefully understaffed and responses to be functionally indistinguishable from

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.360
automated responses

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:30.119
Still the fact that they are offering that type of support and access to the volunteers entering subtitles has rightly pissed off many content creators

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:34.380
Many of whom have decade-old channels in good standing, hundreds of thousands of subscribers,

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:41.340
but still have trouble ever contacting a real person over serious issues like fraudulent and malicious takedown orders

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:46.880
And this is why I say the biggest issue of YouTube heroes is a failure to read the optics of the situation

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:53.240
The goal of YouTube heroes is to get more people consistently taking care of boring grunt work like entering captions and subtitles

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:55.960
That one thing right there is at the core of it.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:58.360
Go back and look at the XP rewards for each activity

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.560
one point for correctly flagged video

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:05.720
Meaning that you flagged it and a youtube employee confirmed it was in fact porn or animal abuse.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.440
10 points for being the best answer poster on a forum thread

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.680
or one point per line of accepted captioning or subtitling.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:18.700
For a reference point, my No Man's Sky review has over a hundred and thirty lines of captions

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:23.180
Reporting things like snuff films and pornography and nudity that's not properly age gated:

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:26.550
that's also grunt work crap that they just need more people doing

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:30.080
But at the end of the day, it's all about those captions and subtitles

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.870
That's where all of the XP is

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:36.340
which you may notice is a very boring and unsexy job.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:40.360
See captions and subtitles should be the responsibility of content creators.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:46.820
In broadcast it is the responsibility of the producers to deliver appropriate closed captioning and regionalised versions of their content

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.820
whether that be dubbed or subtitled,

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:51.900
but YouTube doesn't have the leverage to demand that people do that

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:53.820
They're not Netflix or Hulu

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:56.120
so it falls to a volunteer basis.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:58.280
And this is one of the holes of capitalism

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:05.620
Accessibility options are rarely directly profitable enough for producers to invest in without being compelled by an outside force

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:10.580
YouTube already isn't profitable at all for all but a tiny sliver of users

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.920
I'm not talking about the 1%.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:17.560
I'm talking about the point zero zero zero one percent

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:21.140
Compounding this, accessibility is only valuable at saturation.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.970
If 1 percent of popular English videos have Spanish subtitles

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.429
It's not going to draw in more Spanish users

00:07:26.429 --> 00:07:32.900
But if someone can click on any given front page video and have pretty reasonable odds that there will be Spanish subtitles

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.440
that changes the value.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.740
Same thing with closed captioning for the hearing impaired

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:41.360
It's such a monumental task that it's not financially feasible to hire people to do it.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.500
Years worth of videos are uploaded every day

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:49.240
They would never be able to catch up even if they only stuck to the few thousand most popular videos on any given day

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.960
So it's a thing that has very low market value

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:57.940
But a huge value to the people who make use of it, people who don't speak the dominant language, or who are hearing impaired.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:02.380
Incentivizing volunteer captioners isn't the worst idea in the world

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:05.900
YouTube does technically stand to benefit monetarily from the effort

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:08.540
But at the end of the day, not that much

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:15.080
So the reality that we live in is that either a volunteer force donates their time to improving accessibility,

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:17.040
Or it never gets done

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:23.360
So youTube did something sensible, they took a boring job and they dressed it up in a fancy suit and added prizes

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:30.380
Where they failed was specifically in considering how the framing of those prizes would be perceived by the content creators who have long been

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:34.660
frustrated by the lack of diverse and meaningful moderation tools at their disposal

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.820
That super tool, the one that grants you moderation powers?

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:41.700
Remember that no one knows YouTube Creator Community is even a thing

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.480
so watching this

00:08:56.280 --> 00:09:01.260
Is it any wonder that people just assumed they were going to hand out site-wide comment

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:02.790
moderation power to randos?

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:04.080
How does that look?

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:10.940
I as a channel owner still can't deputize comment moderators like I can on Twitch, Discourse, Wordpress, Reddit, or Discuss

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:14.260
without giving them full access to the entire YouTube account.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:19.400
And you're just going to hand out powers to people who get enough points playing your minigame?

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:23.920
Well, it's no surprise that people interpreted it that way and immediately got pissed off.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.640
Having said that though,

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:29.700
while it is totally understandable, and I do not in any way want to down play

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:34.580
the very real complaints that content creators have about the poor resources available to them,

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:40.159
at the end of the day this Youtube heroes program is an okay idea.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:48.300
It jus- it needs a bit of tweaking and some much much much better communication about what exactly they're giving people power to do.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:49.820
(whispered) Like share subscribe

